      "In his classic 1949 essay 'The Land Ethic', the ecologist Aldo Leopold identified the root philosophical delusion underlying industrial destruction: modern civilisation regards the land merely as an inert commodity belonging to us, rather than as a living biotic community to which we belong. So long as nature is valued exclusively through market price tags, ecosystems remain defenceless against short-term liquidation.",
