    "texte": [
      "Convening at the European Parliament's forum on ecological governance in Brussels, the environmental sociologist Dr Clara Vermeulen and the public-policy strategist Professor Thomas Albright confronted one of the sharpest strategic tensions within contemporary political ecology: should the ecological movement pursue uncompromising systemic radicalism—demanding rapid structural transformation through civil disobedience and post-capitalist rupture—or embrace patient institutional pragmatism, working inside ministries, regulatory agencies, and market mechanisms to secure incremental decarbonisation? 'Across the past thirty years, polite incremental diplomacy has produced dozens of international climate summits while global greenhouse gas emissions climbed by over sixty percent,' Dr Vermeulen opened. 'When vested fossil-fuel lobbies capture legislative agendas, radical grassroots mobilisation and disruptive civil disobedience become the indispensable historical catalysts that force entrenched institutions to confront reality.'",
