"Around the world, however, courageous communities are proving that linguistic homogenisation is neither inevitable nor irreversible: from Māori immersion schools in Aotearoa New Zealand and Welsh media revitalisation to indigenous digital lexicography projects across the Americas and Africa, grassroots movements are reclaiming ancestral tongues as vibrant vehicles of contemporary science, poetry, and civic life.",
