"Therefore, before this assembly, I call upon governments, educational institutions, and technology regulators to protect linguistic plurality as a fundamental human right: guaranteeing mother-tongue-based multilingual education from early childhood through university; requiring global digital platforms and artificial intelligence developers to support indigenous and minority languages equitably under community governance; and recognising that every language preserved from extinction keeps alive an irreplaceable human way of wondering at the world."
