"It is particularly wry to observe the selective economic orthodoxy preached to African policymakers during monetary-reform debates today: international financial institutions that celebrate flexible exchange rates and active central-bank industrial support in Washington, Frankfurt, or Tokyo solemnly warn African governments that exercising identical monetary autonomy would inevitably unleash hyperinflationary ruin.",
